        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Air France flight to US diverted to Montreal due to Ebola travel restrictions Issued on: 22/05/2026 - 17:40 An Air France flight bound for Detroit was diverted to Montreal after a passenger from the Congo boarded a flight in Paris “in error” amid flight restrictions tied to the Ebola outbreak, US Customs and Border Protection said Thursday. A spokesperson for the agency says the passenger “should not have boarded” the plane Wednesday due to US entry restrictions put in place to reduce the risk of Ebola spreading. Naïka in Cannes: A conversation around self-confidence and cinema 22/05/2026 Gaza flotilla: Activists allege abuse, sexual assault on return from Israel 22/05/2026 Trump says ‘it looks like I’ll be the one’ to intervene in Cuba after Castro indictment 22/05/2026 REPLAY: US Secretary of State Marco Rubio speaks to the press at NATO meeting 22/05/2026 Cubans gather before US embassy in Havana to protest Raul Castro indictment 22/05/2026 Cannes Film Festival 2026: FRANCE 24's journalists share their favourites 22/05/2026 Israel deports hundreds of Gaza flotilla activists after international backlash 22/05/2026 Ukraine boosts border security with Belarus over attack fears 22/05/2026 REPLAY: NATO foreign ministers meet in Sweden 22/05/2026"
